WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.647
<v DANA>Here's a quick one about a used blade.
Say you've just finished a blade change,

00:00:04.647 --> 00:00:08.400
<v DANA>and the old blade is still in your hand.
What do you do with it?

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:13.508
<v RAY>Well, you might want to set it down for a
minute, or drop it in the nearest trash

00:00:13.508 --> 00:00:15.360
<v RAY>can. But NEITHER one is safe.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.840
<v DANA>[skeptical] Why not, if it's only for a
minute?

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.208
<v RAY>[matter-of-fact] Because a used blade is
a hazard even when it looks clean. The

00:00:22.208 --> 00:00:25.680
<v RAY>next person who reaches for that spot, or
that bag, is at risk.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.080
<v DANA>So what's the right way to handle it?

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.342
<v RAY>There are four steps. One, know your
route to a sharps container before you

00:00:33.342 --> 00:00:38.818
<v RAY>start. Two, use a safer tool if one will
do the job. Three, turn on the safety

00:00:38.818 --> 00:00:44.151
<v RAY>feature if there is one. Four, put the
used blade straight into a designated

00:00:44.151 --> 00:00:45.360
<v RAY>sharps container.

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:49.556
<v DANA>[playful] I guess that sounds simple
enough. Does it change if the container

00:00:49.556 --> 00:00:50.240
<v DANA>is far away?

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:55.461
<v RAY>No, it doesn't. Actually, the whole rule
comes down to this: a used blade goes

00:00:55.461 --> 00:00:57.360
<v RAY>STRAIGHT into the container.

